64
00:02:15,896 --> 00:02:16,981
That's what a radian means.

65
00:02:17,806 --> 00:02:19,976
For a small angle, the height, sine x,

66
00:02:20,117 --> 00:02:21,785
is almost the same as that arc.

67
00:02:22,549 --> 00:02:24,978
So near zero, sine x is close to

68
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:25,380
x,

69
00:02:25,962 --> 00:02:27,067
and the slope there is one.

70
00:02:28,454 --> 00:02:31,506
In degrees, the same graph gets stretched sideways

71
00:02:31,567 --> 00:02:33,133
by about fifty seven point three.

72
00:02:33,815 --> 00:02:36,621
A sideways stretch divides every slope, at matching

73
00:02:36,661 --> 00:02:38,125
points, by that number.

74
00:02:38,928 --> 00:02:40,912
So the slope at zero would be only

75
00:02:40,973 --> 00:02:42,817
about point zero one seven five.

76
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,956
The rule only works with x in radians.

77
00:02:46,704 --> 00:02:47,899
Now the cosine curve.

78
00:02:48,564 --> 00:02:50,435
At zero, it's at a peak, so its

79
00:02:50,476 --> 00:02:51,321
